
# domain
- GameBanana submission means the target GameBanana mod or project page that receives uploaded release files and release updates.
- GameBanana file row means the uploaded file record identified by GameBanana's file row id and used in public mmdl download links.

## authentication
- Playwright storage state contains cookies plus per-origin localStorage and can optionally include IndexedDB when captured with indexedDB enabled. @implemented

# project
- gitbanana is intended to provide reusable GitHub Actions automation for syncing GitHub Releases with GameBanana submissions. @implemented

# research

## github-actions
- GitHub Actions metadata for this project must use action.yml because GitHub Marketplace release visibility is tied to the metadata filename used by released action versions. @implemented
- GitHub Actions JavaScript actions can run on node24 and declare their executable entry point through runs.main. @implemented
- GitHub Actions required inputs are metadata only; the action implementation must validate required inputs explicitly and fail fast with clear errors. @implemented
- Comparable release-upload actions expose a narrow input and output contract, including release tag or file inputs and public artifact or release identifiers as outputs. @implemented

## gamebanana
- External search did not identify an established public GameBanana GitHub Action for release upload, so gitbanana should treat GameBanana publishing as its own core implementation rather than a thin wrapper around a known action. @draft

## sweet-cookie
- sweet-cookie is a local TypeScript cookie extraction tool with a Chrome extension that can export cookies as JSON or base64 CDP-ish cookie payloads. @draft
- sweet-cookie's extension export format includes top-level metadata and a cookies array with name, value, domain, path, secure, httpOnly, sameSite, and expires fields. @draft

# decisions

## scope
- gitbanana's core action must own GameBanana publishing and verification only; GitHub Release creation and GitHub asset upload belong in caller workflows or example templates. @implemented
- Caller workflows are responsible for building release assets and preparing release notes before invoking the GameBanana publish action. @implemented
- gitbanana example workflows are documentation templates and must not become a second implementation path for publishing behavior. @implemented

## inputs
- The GameBanana publish action must require submission-id, asset, release-tag, and release-notes inputs. @implemented
- The GameBanana publish action may accept release-name, api-section, page-section, browser, and auth/session inputs as optional configuration. @implemented

## authentication
- The GameBanana publish action must not treat username/password login as a supported CI authentication path because GameBanana anti-bot protections reject it on GitHub-hosted runners. @implemented
- The GameBanana publish action must support stored browser session authentication as the primary CI authentication path. @implemented
- The GameBanana publish action must authenticate with stored Playwright storage state, not username/password or cookie-only payloads. @implemented
- Playwright storage state and cookie-only payloads are not fully interchangeable because storage state can preserve origin storage that a cookie-only payload cannot. @implemented
- The GameBanana publish action must accept only Playwright storage state authentication inputs, not cookie-only payloads. @implemented
- Cookie-only authentication support is intentionally excluded from gitbanana because it is less complete than Playwright storage state and would expand the auth surface. @implemented
- The storage-state capture command must verify that the authenticated browser can reach the target GameBanana edit form before printing or writing secret material for CI. @implemented

## documentation
- The GameBanana publish action must document an easy user workflow for obtaining a Playwright storage state secret for GameBanana. @implemented
- gitbanana must ship a small local capture command that opens a headed browser on the target GameBanana edit page, lets the user complete auth manually, verifies edit access, and emits a gzipped base64 Playwright storage-state secret. @implemented
- The storage-state capture tutorial must not require users to hand-write Playwright scripts. @implemented
- gitbanana's complete example release workflow must show building an asset, preparing release notes, running gitbanana, creating or updating the GitHub Release, and optionally uploading debug artifacts on failure. @implemented
- gitbanana documentation must include both concise README snippets and a complete example release workflow. @implemented

## idempotency
- gitbanana publish action reruns must fail with a clear diagnostic when an existing GameBanana update for the release is linked to the wrong file instead of silently repairing or deleting remote GameBanana history. @implemented
- gitbanana publish action reruns must be idempotent for the same release-tag when the existing GameBanana update is already linked to a matching active file. @implemented

## submission-types
- gitbanana must support multiple GameBanana submission types through explicit api-section and page-section inputs. @implemented
- gitbanana must not infer GameBanana api-section or page-section from a GameBanana URL because API section names and page route names are separate explicit inputs. @implemented
- gitbanana must default api-section to Mod and page-section to mods. @implemented

## release-notes
- gitbanana must not include a full Markdown or HTML rendering pipeline for release notes in the core action. @implemented
- gitbanana must parse release note bullets into GameBanana changelog entries with simple heading-based category mapping. @implemented
- gitbanana must accept release notes as Markdown text and convert them to GameBanana update HTML with a deliberately small deterministic renderer. @implemented
- gitbanana's Markdown-to-GameBanana renderer must support headings, bullet lists, and paragraphs, and must HTML-escape user-provided text by default. @implemented

## outputs
- gitbanana must expose file-id, file-url, update-id, and already-published outputs from the publish action. @implemented
- gitbanana's file-url output must be the public GameBanana mmdl URL derived from the published file-id. @implemented
- gitbanana must not expose raw GameBanana API payloads as action outputs because that would create an unstable public contract. @implemented

## debugging
- gitbanana must collect sanitized debug artifacts into a caller-configurable debug-dir when publishing fails. @implemented
- gitbanana debug artifacts and logs must redact known secret values and must never log raw Playwright storage state. @implemented
- gitbanana must not upload debug artifacts itself; caller workflows own any actions/upload-artifact step and retention policy. @implemented

## language
- gitbanana must use TypeScript for the GitHub Action and capture CLI because GitHub JavaScript actions run directly on Node, Playwright is first-class in Node, and npx-based local capture is ergonomic for users. @implemented
- gitbanana must use a TypeScript JavaScript action compiled to dist/index.js, plus a TypeScript CLI entry for capture. @implemented
- gitbanana must not use a polyglot architecture unless a later requirement creates a concrete need that TypeScript cannot cover cleanly. @implemented

## tooling
- gitbanana must use pnpm as its package manager. @implemented
- gitbanana should avoid Bun-specific runtime behavior because GitHub Action execution and Playwright action packaging are standardized around Node. @implemented
- gitbanana must target the Node GitHub Action runtime even though the repository package manager is pnpm. @implemented

## testing
- gitbanana browser-facing tests should use local Playwright fixture pages to exercise edit-form detection and upload-row promotion without writing to GameBanana. @implemented
- gitbanana may provide an opt-in manual smoke workflow for real GameBanana publishing verification gated by required secrets. @implemented
- gitbanana normal CI must not perform live GameBanana publishing writes by default. @implemented
- gitbanana tests must cover pure behavior including input validation, storage-state decoding, release-note conversion, update and file matching, idempotency decisions, and output construction. @implemented

## browser
- gitbanana must default the publish action browser backend to cloakbrowser for stealth-oriented GameBanana browser automation. @implemented
- gitbanana may support chromium as an explicit fallback browser backend for local debugging and lower-dependency environments. @implemented

## egress
- The GameBanana publish action can route browser and API traffic through an optional HTTP, HTTPS, or SOCKS5 proxy. @implemented
- gitbanana documentation warns that GitHub-hosted runner IPs can be rejected by GameBanana and shows Tailscale exit-node setup as the recommended hosted-runner egress path. @implemented

# risks

## scope
- Risk: adding project-specific build, changelog parsing, or version derivation to the core action would make it harder to reuse and maintain. @draft

## authentication
- Risk: using sweet-cookie as a runtime dependency inside GitHub Actions would not solve CI authentication because sweet-cookie reads local browser profiles and CI runners do not have the user's authenticated GameBanana browser profile. @draft

## language
- Language-selection risk: a composite shell action would make gitbanana's browser automation, storage-state handling, API polling, and release-note conversion harder to test and easier to turn into shell glue. @draft

# documentation
- gitbanana README uses the provided logo, follows the user's recent concise product README style, and documents purpose, quickstart, authentication capture, inputs, outputs, reruns, debugging, workflows, and local development. @implemented
- gitbanana README includes centered status badges matching the user's kagi README badge style for release, npm, ci, and license. @implemented

# tooling

## gitignore
- gitbanana ignores local dependencies, coverage, editor and OS noise, private environment files, captured GameBanana storage-state secrets, temporary Playwright auth state, local Dora indexes, and local Residue runtime state while keeping distributable dist bundles tracked for the GitHub Action. @implemented

# publishing

## github
- gitbanana is published as the public GitHub repository Microck/gitbanana with repository description and topics that identify it as a GameBanana release publishing GitHub Action. @implemented

## ci
- gitbanana CI passes on the pushed GitHub main branch before npm publishing is treated as complete. @implemented

## npm
- gitbanana is published to npm as the gitbanana package with the repository's current package version. @implemented

## marketplace
- gitbanana action metadata uses the Marketplace-facing action name gitbanana-release and clear upload/release branding for GitHub Marketplace publication. @implemented
